#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329695 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161965 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f1ec99-e166-5986-a07d-f07be0dfeb31" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0166ede7-ac8b-5aee-a3fc-ae0a17866fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326949} {:answer/id #uuid "2ccc7768-32ec-5947-9670-1ec97e53d1da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327328} {:answer/id #uuid "54c6de8d-19a8-57aa-96b2-7a92b017ceaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327667} {:answer/id #uuid "57b8eae7-5346-50fa-98a2-5cd486bfdba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327701} {:answer/id #uuid "ddddd82a-3c70-51bf-a2eb-edddccc2e4c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-4{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0166ede7-ac8b-5aee-a3fc-ae0a17866fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326949} :answer-field/id #uuid "326f90b0-553c-55c5-999d-072fa4528fa2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329280}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5b4f6183-748c-523a-a6b7-35464ca87075" :question/math-academy-id "q-42918" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 21 & 17 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -18 & -13 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations \n\n- ${R}_{1}:=…$\n- ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$\n- ${R}_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the missing elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make entries above and below ${a}_{34}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 & 1 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 21 & 17 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 21 & 17 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 21 & 17 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -18 & -13 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, the missing elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+4{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{4}:={R}_{4}-3{R}_{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162571 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161965 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "21f1ec99-e166-5986-a07d-f07be0dfeb31" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 4x4 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a06f6793-9576-5ae5-ab84-eab51b33dbd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{2}:=R_{2} + R_{1}$ and $R_{4}:=R_{4} - 2R_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160719} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f8b085-4047-57d7-9308-5cce86dbd745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{2}:=R_{2} + R_{1}$ and $R_{4}:=R_{4} + 2R_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160720} {:answer/id #uuid "cad4ea57-8735-520c-b9df-f8006641b304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{2}:=R_{2} - R_{1}$ and $R_{4}:=R_{4} - 2R_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160721} {:answer/id #uuid "521ce4ee-f8bb-59cb-85cb-1406c1d5df0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{2}:=R_{2} - R_{1}$ and $R_{4}:=R_{4} + 2R_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160722} {:answer/id #uuid "70bcfea9-c720-5543-bf05-f807de5b5a2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{2}:=R_{2} - R_{1}$ and $R_{4}:=R_{4} + R_{1}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160723}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e74b3ec1-2373-5bb2-a7c0-3b89ca09fc79" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160718}] :question/id #uuid "e471ec15-a8b3-57bf-a5ff-3531b5523c10" :question/math-academy-id "q-91171" :question/problem "$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 10 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 8 & 7 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & 9\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 13 & 14 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & -14 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $B$ above. By applying three matrix elementary row operations\n\n1. $R_{2}:=…$\n2. $R_{3}:=R_{3} + R_{1}$\n3. $R_{4}:=…$\n\neach of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i} + kR_{1}$, the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B$. What are the missing elementary row operations?"}]}
